---
layout: changelog
title: "Use native Request and Response objects in JavaScript functions"
date: 2026-11-24
cover: /images/blog/announcing-native-request-response/cover.avif
tags: functions
---

JavaScript functions on Node.js 18 and later, Bun, and Deno now work with the Fetch API `Request` and `Response` classes. [`context.req.raw`](/docs/products/functions/develop#native-request) returns the incoming request as a `Request`, and a function can [return a `Response`](/docs/products/functions/develop#native-response) instead of calling a `context.res` method.

```js
export default async ({ req }) => {
    const form = await req.raw.formData();

    return new Response(`Hello, ${form.get('name')}!`);
};
```

Frameworks built on the Fetch API, such as Hono, also run in a function without an adapter. `context.req` and the `context.res` methods work as before.

